{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And Jacob went out</b> Eleven: this pericope is closed (for in all the sedarim there is neither open nor closed). The reason: because he went out secretly and fled in hiding. Above it is written to him for a wife, and adjacent to it <b>And Jacob went out</b> — that he went out to take a wife." "<b> ויצא יעקב מבאר</b> in gematria: His splendor departed, His majesty and His beauty." "<b> יעקב מבאר שבע</b> ס\"ת: עבר, who was hidden in Beth Eber." "<b> ויצא יעקב מבאר שבע</b> ס\"ת: ארבע." "<b> מבאר שבע</b> ס\"ת: ער. And the shin of שבע, ten. שי\"ד two: hidden in Beth Eber." "<b> מבאר שבע</b> ר\"ת: שם, for he too was hidden in the house of Shem." "<b> וילך</b> in gematria: בו ביום."], :book :genesis, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {0 "The phrase 'אין בכל הסדרה' likely refers to the parashah divisions in the annual cycle; rendered 'sedarim' to preserve the technical term.", 1 "The equated phrase פנה זיוה הודה והדרה is rendered as a statement about divine glory departing, matching the gematria value.", 2 "ס\"ת = סופי תיבות (final letters). The referent of עבר is the patriarch Eber, in whose house Jacob hid.", 4 "The notation שי\"ד (= 314) likely combines a letter-value reading with a gematria; the text is terse and possibly compressed. Rendered hyper-literally.", 5 "ר\"ת = ראשי תיבות (initial letters). The initial letters of מבאר שבע spell משב, but he reads it as שם by a reordering or alternative extraction."}, :source-witnesses [["Kitzur Baal HaTurim" "http://sefaria.org"] ["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:17:21.448680875Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}